Non-penetration must be stiff for every material. Scaling contact compliance by softness jams the system. Softness belongs in internal deformation, not in whether two regions can overlap.
"Overdamped" means little carried momentum, not heavy damping — I had it backwards, and it sloshed.
The thixotropic ξ mechanism is load-bearing. Frictionless frustrated packings creep forever; ξ rebuilding at rest to arrest sub-yield creep is the physical settle. The metaphor turned out to be the mechanism — which is exactly the bet the whole project makes.
Initial conditions matter enormously — jittered grid, not jammed clump.

